1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,025
Over 450 million US dollars is lost every year due to faulty

2
00:00:05,060 --> 00:00:10,270
procurement means. Through Quorum, we seek to address this challenge.

3
00:00:10,520 --> 00:00:11,810
Let me show you how it works.

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:14,350
We start on the supplier side.

5
00:00:14,960 --> 00:00:19,225
The portal keeps the required documents together, so it's clear what needs

6
00:00:19,260 --> 00:00:20,410
to be submitted.

7
00:00:21,280 --> 00:00:25,205
Here I'm opening a tax registration certificate and running the AI document

8
00:00:25,240 --> 00:00:30,305
check. Our Meta-powered tool reads the document and checks it against

9
00:00:30,340 --> 00:00:31,890
the requested requirement.

10
00:00:33,020 --> 00:00:36,905
The findings appear beside the original file, making the details easy

11
00:00:36,940 --> 00:00:41,450
to compare. That gives the reviewer a useful starting point.

12
00:00:42,180 --> 00:00:44,830
It doesn't decide whether the supplier qualifies.

13
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:48,290
Now, let's move into the officer's workspace.

14
00:00:48,700 --> 00:00:52,385
This is the same procurement process from the notice and mandatory

15
00:00:52,420 --> 00:00:55,030
requirements through to bid opening and evaluation.

16
00:00:55,800 --> 00:00:58,370
The criteria are set before the bids are assessed.

17
00:00:59,020 --> 00:01:05,765
In this example, technical capability carries 60% and delivery carries 40%.

18
00:01:05,800 --> 00:01:08,570
Officers can check the scores alongside the evidence.

19
00:01:09,060 --> 00:01:12,585
Everything stays in one tender file, so the next person can follow

20
00:01:12,620 --> 00:01:16,005
the reasoning without having to piece it together from separate spreadsheets

21
00:01:16,040 --> 00:01:16,870
and messages.

22
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:20,530
Next, we run the AI assisted bid review.

23
00:01:21,460 --> 00:01:25,545
We include every admitted bidder, confirm consent, and review their

24
00:01:25,580 --> 00:01:27,630
submissions against the issued criteria.

25
00:01:28,720 --> 00:01:30,290
The review is read only.

26
00:01:30,940 --> 00:01:34,290
Here you can see both bidders compared against the same requirements.

27
00:01:35,300 --> 00:01:38,285
When the documents don't establish a required reference contract

28
00:01:38,320 --> 00:01:42,650
or a committed delivery plan, the result says not evidenced.

29
00:01:43,160 --> 00:01:45,090
It doesn't fill in the gap.

30
00:01:45,940 --> 00:01:49,550
Instead, it gives the committee specific questions to follow up.

31
00:01:50,060 --> 00:01:51,690
Can we verify these references?

32
00:01:52,200 --> 00:01:54,030
Are the delivery milestones clear?

33
00:01:54,920 --> 00:01:57,490
Does the price build up support the proposal?

34
00:01:58,280 --> 00:02:00,030
That is where the AI helps.

35
00:02:00,880 --> 00:02:04,005
It prepares a clearer review so people can spend their time checking

36
00:02:04,040 --> 00:02:04,870
what matters.

37
00:02:05,864 --> 00:02:12,110
The AI presents the strongest documented fit for the committee consideration.

38
00:02:13,660 --> 00:02:15,870
It then evaluates both sides.

39
00:02:16,480 --> 00:02:18,430
It then submits information to the committee.

40
00:02:19,180 --> 00:02:22,665
Based off of information that it will give you as a committee,

41
00:02:22,700 --> 00:02:24,430
you then proceed to then select.

42
00:02:25,550 --> 00:02:30,985
So as a committee, you have the ability to set up what

43
00:02:31,020 --> 00:02:36,165
we call the full committee that has to make up their own

44
00:02:36,200 --> 00:02:39,610
decision. This is a panel of the committee.

45
00:02:40,100 --> 00:02:44,365
We can add any other person to the committee to constitute

46
00:02:44,400 --> 00:02:49,105
the quorum, who then makes the final decision in terms of who

47
00:02:49,140 --> 00:02:50,750
to award a particular contract.

48
00:02:51,500 --> 00:02:54,430
Each person has to have the verdict signed.

49
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:58,045
The evaluation record stays visible too.

50
00:02:58,080 --> 00:03:02,390
Officers can inspect the evaluator sheets, differences in scores,

51
00:03:03,060 --> 00:03:04,470
and the recorded consensus.

52
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:08,150
The AI doesn't write those scores or award the tender.

53
00:03:08,700 --> 00:03:11,825
The committee records its assessment and authorised people make

54
00:03:11,860 --> 00:03:15,745
the decision. Award, contract and complaint records remain connected

55
00:03:15,780 --> 00:03:16,930
to the same file.

56
00:03:17,500 --> 00:03:20,565
So the team can explain both what it decided and the evidence

57
00:03:20,600 --> 00:03:21,870
behind that decision.

58
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:26,270
We've also published Quorum's MCP integration.

59
00:03:27,280 --> 00:03:31,725
It lets compatible AI clients connect to our read-only tools, bringing

60
00:03:31,760 --> 00:03:34,830
this evidence into the tools teams already use.

61
00:03:35,780 --> 00:03:37,690
The boundaries stay the same.

62
00:03:38,440 --> 00:03:42,630
The AI helps prepare the work and authorized people keep control.

63
00:03:43,800 --> 00:03:46,270
That's Quorum. The agent prepares the file.

64
00:03:47,140 --> 00:03:49,170
The committee awards the tender.
